      "why": "iterative is the smallest-area family (single datapath, no pipeline registers). It is the only family that can plausibly minimise luts_plus_ffs while meeting max_abs_err <= 2^-10. data_width 12-16 and n_iter 10-16 cover the accuracy sweet spot; angle_guard -2..0 and frac_guard 0..1 keep area low without sacrificing the 10-bit error budget."
    }
  ,
    {
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "ranges": [
        {
          "param": "data_width",
          "low": 12,
          "high": 16
        ,
          "choices": null
        },
        {
